    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      175.87,
      203.09,
      397.19,
      260.75
    ],
    "text": "(b) high ethical standards in business and professions;the recognition of the worthiness of all usefuloccupations and the dignifying of each Foundationmember\u2019s occupation as an opportunity to servesociety;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      176.71,
      270.41,
      397.18,
      304.79
    ],
    "text": "(c) the application of the ideal of service in eachFoundation member\u2019s personal, business andcommunity life;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      175.87,
      314.45,
      397.2,
      360.23
    ],
    "text": "(d) the advancement of international understanding,goodwill and peace through a world fellowship ofbusiness and professional persons united in the idealof service;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      176.71,
      369.89,
      397.19,
      392.75
    ],
    "text": "(e) developmet and encouragement of religiousharmony through community service orientation;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      178.15,
      402.41,
      387.47,
      413.75
    ],
    "text": "(f) open discussion of all matters of public interest;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      175.87,
      423.41,
      397.17,
      457.67
    ],
    "text": "(g) to do all such acts and things as may be necessaryfor the accomplishment of all or any of the objectsof the Corporation;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      175.87,
      467.33,
      397.19,
      536.27
    ],
    "text": "(h) to aid and assist any person to engage himself inany Industry, Trade or Import or Export business toestablish and maintain any Agricultural, Industrialor Commercial \u201cVentures\u201d, to provide programmesto successfully train persons in technical skills andto organize propaganda works;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      178.15,
      545.93,
      397.2,
      568.67
    ],
    "text": "(i) to establish local and international Branches torealize the objects of the Corporation.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      580.37,
      397.3,
      672.59
    ],
    "text": "4.(1) The affairs of the Corporation shall subject to therules of the Corporation, be administered by a Board ofDirectors consisting of members not less than five and notmore than nine in number. Dr. Mervyn DhanawardhanaGuruge shall be the founder Executive President and lifeExecutive President of the Corporation. ShamindaDhanawardhana Guruge and Indika Dhanawardhana Gurugeshall be Vice Presidents for life.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
